<title>UK: BIL sets 150 mln euro six-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>BIL sets 150 mln euro six-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers BIL and CCB.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANQUE INTERNATIONALE A LUXEMBOURG SA</p>
<p> AMT    150 MLN EURO  COUPON     5.50 PCT  MATURITY    30.APR.03</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.70    PAY DATE    30.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    101.70    SPREAD	+12 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 1-10	SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC   1.75</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>UNTIL THE START OF THE THIRD STAGE OF EMU, ALL MONETARY RIGHTS AND OBLIGATIONS IN RESPECT OF THE NOTES SHALL BE DEEMED TO BE DENOMINATED IN ECU AT THE RATE OF ONE ECU FOR ONE EURO.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
